# Directory Structure Guide

The project follows a modular structure under the `src/` directory. Key directories and their purposes:

- [`src/config/`](mdc:src/config): Configuration files and environment setup
- [`src/db/`](mdc:src/db): Database connection logic (MongoDB, Redis)
- [`src/modules/`](mdc:src/modules): Feature modules, each with its own routes, controller, service, and schema
- [`src/routes/`](mdc:src/routes): API route definitions and registration
- [`src/utils/`](mdc:src/utils): Utility functions and helpers
- [`src/middleware/`](mdc:src/middleware): Custom middleware functions

## Feature Organization
Each feature/module should be placed in its own subdirectory under [`src/modules/`](mdc:src/modules), containing:
- `[feature].routes.js`
- `[feature].controller.js`
- `[feature].service.js`
- `[feature].schema.js`
- `__tests__/` (unit and integration tests)

Refer to [`HowToWriteAPI.md`](mdc:HowToWriteAPI.md) for more details on adding new features.
